+  page: it does not remove content, it narrows the region viewers show and
+  `render_page/3` rasterises. Setting the **media box** changes the page's
+  physical size. Mutates `doc` in place and returns `{:ok, doc}`.
+
+      # crop 36pt off every edge of a US Letter page
+      {:ok, doc} = ExPdfium.set_page_box(doc, 0, :crop,
+                     %{left: 36, bottom: 36, right: 576, top: 756})
+
+  The change takes effect **immediately**, with no save-and-reopen round trip:
+  `page_info/2` reports the new `:width`/`:height` and `render_page/3` rasterises
+  the new region on the very next call, byte-for-byte identically to a reopened
+  copy. That makes an interactive crop — adjust, re-render, adjust again — a
+  sequence of calls on one open document.
+
+  Errors:
+    * `:unsupported_box` — `box` is not one of the five settable boxes
